2ksbox (M5h, doc 17 §9): a host drive's sectors are read off the main loop.

A guest's read of the real CD drive (`hostcd:`) ran on QEMU's main loop,
and a read there waits out the drive's seek: 0.18 s on the first drive
(USB), 2.7 s when it spins up from audio to data speed. The whole machine
froze with it whenever a game loaded data during its CD music (XP, Moto
Racer; the user).

For a disc libdisc says is a host drive (`libdisc_is_host_drive`), the
model's sector reads of READ(10) and READ CD, PIO and DMA alike, go to the
thread pool into a buffer of the request's own, holding a reference to the
disc of its own (`libdisc_ref`), since the disc can be swapped out of the
drive meanwhile. The completion runs on the main loop and carries on where
the synchronous loop would have: the burst handed to the guest, the next
DMA chunk, or the failed sector's sense. A reset in between clears
`atapi_disc_pending` and the result is dropped. Images keep the
synchronous path.

READ(10) and PLAY AUDIO check the first sector's kind with
`libdisc_sector_kind`, from the layout, instead of `libdisc_sector_info`,
which reads a drive's sector to verify it.

